WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.767
This query truncates each order timestamp to month grain.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.582
It then groups orders by that month bucket.

00:00:06.582 --> 00:00:11.287
COUNT measures order volume, and SUM calculates monthly revenue.

00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:15.642
The cast to date is mainly for a simpler displayed month label.

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:20.837
The important analytical decision is the month-level grain created by DATE_TRUNC.

00:00:20.837 --> 00:00:28.642
EXTRACT returns a component such as month number or year; DATE_TRUNC returns a timestamp aligned to a time

00:00:28.642 --> 00:00:30.477
boundary such as the start of the month.

00:00:30.477 --> 00:00:39.257
For grouping over multiple years, truncating to month is often safer than grouping by month number alone

00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:43.258
because January 2025 and January 2026 should not be merged accidentally.
